      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Cherry Creek Schoolhouse, built in 1874, sits on the high school campus and is the oldest surviving school building in Greenwood Village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwood_Village%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gold seekers from the East and Midwest settled the area in the 1860s, sparking the early development that would later become Greenwood Village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwood_Village%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1970s saw rapid growth as the Denver Technological Center expanded, turning Greenwood Village into a thriving suburban community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwood_Village%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "When Denver’s boundaries were frozen, Greenwood Village annexed prime properties along I‑25, a move that later prompted Centennial’s incorporation in 2001.",
